  "body": "PR 3 of 5 for OpenProject 2098 (https://openproject.home.romaine.life/wp/2098). Both pickers (terminal and the popup that replaces file dialogs) now show one folder at a time with its full path, and the popup no longer flickers.\n\n- Changed: fzt's scoped view is on and the `:` palette is off. The standalone picker starts at the drive roots and enters `--start-dir`, so you can still go up from it. The popup paints into an off-screen bitmap and copies it in one blit (closes OpenProject 1662). Bumped to fzt-terminal v0.1.102, which includes v0.1.101's fix for the idle full-screen repaint (the terminal flicker).\n- Replaced: both paths now return the selected item's `Original` path, instead of `AcceptNth` and the popup's `SelectedItemPath`, which only works with a cursor row.\n- Added: `publish.ps1` publishes a release to `\\\\NelsonNAS\\tools\\fzt-picker`, replacing the hand-installed copy in `~\\bin`.\n\nTested: standalone picker driven through tmux (enter, go up, scroll, a query that matches nothing, pick). The popup DLL is built by this PR's CI, and is exercised live after publishing.\n",
